  "worked_solution": "Since we need to multiply $\\frac{6}{16}$ by $3$, we repeat the fraction model $3$ times, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129810/assets/df3d9e3f7b3bde5b93ec6a54cd6e4d129a2852bdd9017991853191ad7347eda0.png)\n\n \n\nThere are $3\\times 6=18$ shaded pieces in total. Therefore, \n\n$$\n3\\times \\frac{6}{16}=\\frac{18}{16}.\n$$",
